          "explanation": "<div class=\"ml-en\"><p>$\\hat p = 20/500 = 0.04$. $z_0 = \\dfrac{\\hat p - p_0}{\\sqrt{p_0(1-p_0)/n}} = \\dfrac{0.04-0.03}{\\sqrt{0.03(0.97)/500}} = \\dfrac{0.01}{\\sqrt{0.0000582}} = \\dfrac{0.01}{0.007629} \\approx 1.31$. The test is LEFT-tailed, so we would need $z_0 < -1.65$. Here $z_0 = +1.31$ is not even on the correct side (the sample proportion is ABOVE 0.03), so we do not reject $H_0$.</p></div><div class=\"ml-vi\"><p>$\\hat p = 20/500 = 0{,}04$. $z_0 = \\dfrac{\\hat p - p_0}{\\sqrt{p_0(1-p_0)/n}} = \\dfrac{0{,}04-0{,}03}{\\sqrt{0{,}03(0{,}97)/500}} = \\dfrac{0{,}01}{0{,}007629} \\approx 1{,}31$. Kiểm định là PHÍA TRÁI nên cần $z_0 < -1{,}65$. Ở đây $z_0 = +1{,}31$ thậm chí còn nằm sai phía (tỉ lệ mẫu CAO HƠN 0,03), nên không bác bỏ $H_0$.</p></div>"
